// A data logger with a real time clock and a display: SD_RTCLogger_mega328p.gcb with an ILI9341 (320 x 240)
// that shows the clock, every second, and the data logger: the last sample, the file, lines written and lost.
//
// Setting the clock: on the clock screen (the menu's button 4, below), or from the serial terminal: at the start
// the program shows the DS1307's date and time and waits SET_WAIT (10) s for a line
//     T2026-11-09 14:30:00        (T, then year, month, day, hour, minute, second: 14 digits, any separators)
// ending with Enter. When the clock is not running and no time is sent, the clock screen opens.
//
// What is logged: the ATmega328P's own temperature sensor (ADC channel 8, 1.1 V reference), in whole degrees C
// (the display shield takes A0 .. A3 and the clock A4 / A5, so no analogue pin is free). The sensor is not
// calibrated (the datasheet gives +/- 10 C): set TEMP_OFFSET, below, from a thermometer. Each line is
// "date,time,temperature", eg "2026-11-09,14:30:05,24", heading "Date,Time,ChipC".
// Each tap on the screen is a line too: "date,time,touch,screen,raw x,raw y,button", eg
// "2026-11-09,14:30:07,touch,1,512,480,2": the screen (0 main, 1 menu, 2 black, 3 the clock screen), the panel's raw
// X reading (up and down the screen), its raw Y (across), and the menu button for it (0 the title, 1 .. 4).
// The heading goes in a new file; a line every 5 s on the clock's seconds. The file's date in the folder is the clock's. A card pulled out and
// put back is started again, and a "Restarted" line marks lost samples.
//
// The clock: A4 is both the display's RESET and the DS1307's SDA, so every I2C transfer resets the display (it
// goes blank). So the DS1307 is read only at the start, when it is set, and once an hour (at hh:00:00). In
// between, the program keeps the time itself: Timer1 interrupts once a second, from the 16 MHz crystal (a few
// seconds a day at most; each hourly read puts it right). After each I2C transfer the screen is started again
// (InitGLCD) and drawn again: a short blank once an hour. With the shield's A4 pin lifted and the display's RST
// tied high, the hourly blank goes, but the program does not need that.
//
// Touch (touch_4wire.h): a tap on the screen shows the menu, four buttons across the screen:
//   1  Stop logging / Start logging    while off, the samples and taps are counted and shown, not written
//   2  Rotate screen                   the screen turned round 180 degrees (landscape, landscape reversed)
//   3  Black screen                    all black and nothing drawn, until the next tap (the ILI9341's Display
//                                      Off shows white on this panel)
//   4  Set clock                       the clock screen: the date, the time and the drift, with six buttons
//                                      along the foot: < > (the field), - + (its value), OK (set), X (cancel)
// A tap on the menu's title, or no tap for MENU_WAIT seconds (the clock screen: CLOCK_WAIT), goes back without a
// change. The clock and the logging go on while the menu, the clock screen or the black screen is up.
//
// Drift: the DS1307's crystal is a few ppm (millionths) fast or slow. Set it on the clock screen, in ppm
// (+ the clock gains, - it loses, -250 .. 250): measure it over a week or more, ppm = seconds gained / seconds
// gone * 1000000. Each hour (at hh:00:30) the drift is added up, and each whole second of it moves the DS1307's
// seconds back (or on) by one. The drift and its running total are kept in the DS1307's battery-backed RAM, so a
// reset loses neither. CLOCK_DRIFT is the drift until the clock screen first sets one.
//
// Where a tap is up and down the screen comes from the panel's raw X reading (TOUCH_RAW_Y20 and TOUCH_RAW_Y220),
// and across the screen (the clock screen's buttons) from its raw Y reading (TOUCH_RAW_X20, TOUCH_RAW_X220): from Touch_Calibrate_ILI9341_mega328p.gcb.
// The panel is read between screen updates (it shares the display's RS, CS, DB0 and DB1).
//
// Board: Arduino Uno (ATmega328P, 16 MHz crystal, 5 V) with
//        a Deek-Robot data logging shield v1.0 (SD card at 3V3, DS1307 with a CR1220 battery), and
//        an ILI9341 8-bit UNO display shield
//        ILI9341 RD A0, WR A1, RS A2, CS A3, RESET A4; DB0 D8, DB1 D9, DB2 .. DB7 D2 .. D7
//        Touch   XP D8, XM A2, YP A3, YM D9 (found with Touch_Probe_mega328p.gcb)
//        SPI     SCK D13 (PB5), MOSI D11 (PB3), MISO D12 (PB4); the card's chip select D10 (PB2)
//        I2C     SDA A4 (PC4), SCL A5 (PC5): the DS1307, 100 kHz. A4 is also the display's RESET: see above
//        UART    TX D1, RX D0: the Uno's USB serial port, 9600 8N1: the clock setting, what is logged, any error
// Programming: use.ini's Arduino UNO programmer (avrdude, the Uno's bootloader). Opening the serial port resets
//        the Uno, so the program starts again then (and adds to RTCLOG.CSV).
//
//@author    Evan R. Venn
//@licence   LGPL 2.1
//@date      09/11/2026
//
// Change log
//   09/11/2026  First version: SD_RTCLogger_mega328p.gcb with an ILI9341 8-bit display, logging the chip temperature
//   09/11/2026  FatDate / FatTime in one place, ClockToFat, called by LogWrite before FatCommit
//   09/11/2026  The screen went blank: each DS1307 read (SDA on A4) reset the display (RESET on A4). The time is
//               kept by Timer1 and read from the DS1307 only at the start and hourly; the screen is started
//               again after each read
//   09/11/2026  #option ReserveHighProg OPTIBOOT: a program too large for the space below the bootloader is
//               a compile error, not a programming failure that overwrites the bootloader
//   09/11/2026  Touch: a tap turns the display off and on (touch_4wire.h)
//   09/11/2026  Blank is the screen cleared to black and nothing drawn, not Display Off (white on this panel)
//   09/11/2026  ChipTemp waits 40 ms for the 1.1 V reference: after a touch reading (AVcc) it read 0 C
//   09/11/2026  TEMP_OFFSET 328, from this chip: 350 at 22.5 C (the datasheet's 267 read 84 C)
//   09/11/2026  A double tap turns the screen round 180 degrees (TouchTaps); a single tap blanks it, as before
//   09/11/2026  A tap shows a menu: start / stop logging, rotate the screen, black screen (in place of the taps)
//   09/11/2026  The temperature in each log line again
//   09/11/2026  The drive is started with FatInit() (sd_fat.h 1.2): SDCInit and FatMount in one call
//   10/11/2026  SDA and SCL made inputs before HI2CMode
//   10/11/2026  A tap on the black screen starts the display again (ScreenStart), not only draws it
//   10/11/2026  Each tap is logged (TouchLog): where the panel was pressed and the button that gives
//   10/11/2026  The menu's button edges worked out when compiling (MenuPressed: no 32-bit sums, 220 words less);
//               the touch calibration is the four TOUCH_RAW_X20, X220, Y20, Y220 the calibration program shows
//               (from 10/11/2026: Y20 191, Y220 832)
//   10/11/2026  The LGT8F328P has its own program, SD_RTCLogger_ILI9341_LGT8F328P.gcb: this one is the
//               ATmega328P's only
//   10/11/2026  LOG_AT_START: logging on (LOG_ON) or off (LOG_OFF) at the start; "Not logging" (was
//               "Logging stopped"); while not logging, the samples and taps are still counted and shown
//   11/11/2026  The clock screen (the menu's button 4): the date, the time and the drift set by touch; the drift
//               (ppm, kept in the DS1307's RAM) moves the DS1307 a second at a time, checked hourly at hh:00:30
//               (the hourly read moved from hh:00:00). ClockStore: the checks and the setting, shared by the serial
//               T line and the clock screen; a stopped clock waits SET_WAIT for the T line, then opens the clock
//               screen. Less flash for it all: shorter console messages; the display started by ScreenInit (the
//               library's settings from a table: #define InitGLCD_ILI9341 ScreenInit), boxes by ScreenBox, the
//               DS1307 read and written by DsRead and DsWrite (in place of ds1307.h's routines, one for each
//               register); MenuPressed and the clock screen take one set of edges, the reading turned round

    #option explicit
    #option IncludePath "C:\GCstudio\gcbasic\AdditionalLibraries"

// ----- Chip

    #Chip mega328p, 16
    #option ReserveHighProg OPTIBOOT    // the Uno's bootloader at the top of the flash: 1,024 words kept free

// ----- The display: an ILI9341 on the 8-bit bus

    #include <glcd.h>
    #define GLCD_TYPE GLCD_TYPE_ILI9341
    #define InitGLCD_ILI9341 ScreenInit // the display started by ScreenInit (below), in place of the library's
    #define GLCD_RD       PortC.0           // A0, read
    #define GLCD_WR       PortC.1           // A1, write
    #define GLCD_RS       PortC.2           // A2, command / data
    #define GLCD_CS       PortC.3           // A3, chip select
    #define GLCD_RESET    PortC.4           // A4, reset: also the DS1307's SDA, see above
    #define GLCD_DB0      PortB.0           // D8
    #define GLCD_DB1      PortB.1           // D9
    #define GLCD_DB2      PortD.2           // D2
    #define GLCD_DB3      PortD.3           // D3
    #define GLCD_DB4      PortD.4           // D4
    #define GLCD_DB5      PortD.5           // D5
    #define GLCD_DB6      PortD.6           // D6
    #define GLCD_DB7      PortD.7           // D7

// ----- Serial port: the console, needed to set the clock. 9600: at 16 MHz the AVR's USART is 0.2 % out

    #define USART_BAUD_RATE 9600
    #define USART_BLOCKING

// ----- Pins

    #define SDC_SCK         PortB.5     // D13, SCK
    #define SDC_DO          PortB.3     // D11, MOSI: to the card's DI
    #define SDC_DI          PortB.4     // D12, MISO: from the card's DO
    #define SDC_CS          PortB.2     // D10: the card's chip select, and the AVR's SS pin (so no SDC_SS)

// ----- The clock: a DS1307 on the hardware I2C (TWI)

    #define HI2C_BAUD_RATE  100         // kHz: the DS1307's top speed
    #define HI2C_DATA       PortC.4     // A4, SDA
    #define HI2C_CLOCK      PortC.5     // A5, SCL
    #include <ds1307.h>

// ----- The drive: an SD card on the SPI (sd_card.h picks its AVR shim, sd_card_avr.h)

    #define SDC_SPI_SLOW    MasterSlow  // start-up: Fosc / 64, 250 kHz (the card needs 100 to 400 kHz)
    #define SDC_SPI_FAST    MasterFast  // data: Fosc / 4, 4 MHz
    #include <sd_card.h>
    #include <sd_fat.h>

// ----- Settings

    #define LOG_EVERY       5           // seconds between samples: a divisor of 60 (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 10, 12, 15, 20, 30)
    #define SET_WAIT        10          // seconds to wait for the time at the start (T yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss)
    #define MENU_WAIT       10          // seconds the menu stays up with no tap
    #define CLOCK_WAIT      60          // seconds the clock screen stays up with no tap
    #define CLOCK_DRIFT     0           // ppm, -250 .. 250: the DS1307's drift until the clock screen sets it
    #define LOG_AT_START    LOG_ON      // logging at the start: LOG_ON, or LOG_OFF (the menu's button 1 starts it)
    #define LOG_ON          1
    #define LOG_OFF         0
    #define TEMP_OFFSET     328         // ADC reading at 0 C: this chip read 350 at 22.5 C (the datasheet's typical: 267)

    // what is logged: the chip temperature
    #define SAMPLE_WHAT     "the chip temperature"
    #define SAMPLE_LABEL    "Chip temp"
    #define SAMPLE_UNIT     " C  "
    #define SAMPLE_HEAD     "Date,Time,ChipC"

    // The touch panel (touch_4wire.h): its wires share the display's pins
    #define TOUCH_XP        PortB.0     // D8, the display's DB0
    #define TOUCH_XM        PortC.2     // A2, the display's RS
    #define TOUCH_YP        PortC.3     // A3, the display's CS
    #define TOUCH_YM        PortB.1     // D9, the display's DB1
    #define TOUCH_YP_AN     AN3
    #define TOUCH_XM_AN     AN2         // A2: TouchRawY (across the screen) reads on XM
    // Touch calibration: the panel's raw readings at the screen's x 20 and x 220, y 20 and y 220 (landscape).
    // Run Touch_Calibrate_ILI9341_mega328p.gcb and copy the four #define lines it shows here. On this shield the
    // screen's x is the panel's raw Y (TouchRawY) and its y the raw X (TouchRawX). The menu uses TOUCH_RAW_Y20
    // and TOUCH_RAW_Y220 (its buttons go across the screen); the clock screen's buttons use all four
    #define TOUCH_RAW_X20       868
    #define TOUCH_RAW_X220      360
    #define TOUCH_RAW_Y20       191
    #define TOUCH_RAW_Y220      832
    #include <touch_4wire.h>
    // Worked out when compiling, from the calibration (no 32-bit sums in the program):
    //   the menu's four buttons' top edges (y 28, 82, 136, 190) and the clock screen's row of buttons (from y 170)
    //   as raw X readings; TOUCH_RAW_YSUM, the raw X at y and at 239 - y added (turned round, MenuPressed takes the
    //   reading from it, so the same edges do); the five edges between the clock screen's six buttons across the
    //   screen (x 53, 106, 160, 213, 266, the same turned round) as raw Y readings. This shield's raw Y goes down
    //   as x goes up (X20 more than X220)
    #script
        TOUCH_RAW_B1 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + (28 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_B2 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + (82 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_B3 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + (136 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_B4 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + (190 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_ROW = Int(TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + (170 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        If TOUCH_RAW_Y220 <= TOUCH_RAW_Y20 Then
            Error "The menu needs TOUCH_RAW_Y220 more than TOUCH_RAW_Y20 (this shield's way)"
        End If
        TOUCH_RAW_YSUM = Int(2 * TOUCH_RAW_Y20 + 199 * (TOUCH_RAW_Y220 - TOUCH_RAW_Y20) / 200)
        If TOUCH_RAW_X220 >= TOUCH_RAW_X20 Then
            Error "The clock screen's buttons need TOUCH_RAW_X20 more than TOUCH_RAW_X220 (this shield's way)"
        End If
        TOUCH_RAW_E1 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_X20 - (53 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_X20 - TOUCH_RAW_X220) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_E2 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_X20 - (106 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_X20 - TOUCH_RAW_X220) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_E3 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_X20 - (160 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_X20 - TOUCH_RAW_X220) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_E4 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_X20 - (213 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_X20 - TOUCH_RAW_X220) / 200)
        TOUCH_RAW_E5 = Int(TOUCH_RAW_X20 - (266 - 20) * (TOUCH_RAW_X20 - TOUCH_RAW_X220) / 200)
        If CLOCK_DRIFT < -250 Or CLOCK_DRIFT > 250 Then
            Error "CLOCK_DRIFT is -250 .. 250 ppm"
        End If
        CLOCK_DRIFT_B = CLOCK_DRIFT + 256
    #endscript

    // Screen layout (landscape, 320 x 240) and colours
    #define SCR_BACK        ILI9341_BLACK
    #define SCR_BUTTON      ILI9341_NAVY
    // what is on the screen
    #define SCR_MAIN        0           // the clock and the logger
    #define SCR_MENU        1           // the menu
    #define SCR_BLACK       2           // black, nothing drawn
    #define SCR_SETCLOCK    3           // the clock screen (the menu's button 4). Odd, as SCR_MENU: both time out

    // the DS1307's battery-backed RAM (0x08 .. 0x3F): the drift, its running total, and a mark that they are set
    #define DS_RAM_MARK     0x08        // DS_MARK when the drift and its total are there
    #define DS_RAM_DRIFT    0x09        // 0x09 (low), 0x0A (high): the drift, ppm + 256
    #define DS_RAM_TOTAL    0x0B        // 0x0B (low), 0x0C (high): the drift's running total, in 0.1 ms
    #define DS_MARK         0x5B        // (0x5A was the one-byte drift: not read as this)
    #define SCR_TITLE       ILI9341_CYAN
    #define SCR_CLOCK       ILI9341_WHITE
    #define SCR_TEXT        ILI9341_YELLOW
    #define SCR_GOOD        ILI9341_GREEN
    #define SCR_BAD         ILI9341_RED

    // Timer1: compare match A once a second. 16 MHz / 256 = 62500 counts a second, so OCR1A = 62499
    #define TICK_TOP        62499
    #define TICK_CLOCK      0x0C        // WGM12: CTC, to OCR1A; CS12: clock / 256
    #script
        If ChipMHz <> 16 Then
            Error "TICK_TOP is for 16 MHz: work it out again for this clock"
        End If
    #endscript

// ----- Main program

    Dim RTCHour, RTCMin, RTCSec, RTCDay, RTCMonth, RTCYear As Byte    // the DS1307's time
    Dim DsBuf(7) As Byte                // the DS1307's registers, read or to write (DsRead, DsWrite)
    Dim Sample As Word                  // the sample: the chip temperature, C
    Dim TapCount As Word                // taps since the start (not TouchCount: touch_4wire.h's debounce count)
    Dim TouchRaw As Word                // the last tap: the panel's raw X (MenuPressed)
    Dim LinesWritten, LinesLost As Word // for the display
    Dim LogReady As Bit                 // 1 = the drive is started and RTCLOG.CSV is open
    Dim LogLost As Bit                  // 1 = a sample was not written: a "Restarted" line goes in first
    Dim LogLine As String * 24
    Dim TickCount As Byte               // seconds counted by Timer1, not yet added to the time (ClockTick)
    Dim ClockOK As Bit                  // 1 = the DS1307 is running
    Dim ScrMode As Byte                 // what is on the screen: SCR_MAIN, SCR_MENU or SCR_BLACK
    Dim ScrTurn As Byte                 // the screen's way round: LANDSCAPE or LANDSCAPE_REV (the menu's button 2)
    Dim MenuSecs As Byte                // seconds left before the menu goes
    Dim LogRun As Bit                   // 1 = logging; 0 = stopped (the menu's button 1)
    Dim TouchToFile As Bit              // 1 = this tap goes in the file too (logging, the drive ready)
    Dim MenuRaw As Word                 // the tap's raw X, the screen's way up (MenuPressed)
    Dim ClkRaw As Word                  // the tap's raw Y, across the screen (MenuPressed, for the clock screen)
    Dim ClockDrift As Word              // the drift: ppm + 256 (256 = none, 6 .. 506)
    Dim EdDrift As Word                 // the clock screen's drift, ppm + 256
    Dim DriftTotal As Word              // the drift built up, in 0.1 ms: each 10000 (1 s) moves the DS1307
    Dim EdVal(7) As Byte                // the clock screen: year (00 .. 99), month, day, hour, minute, second (7: EdDrift)
    Dim EdField As Byte                 // the clock screen's field, 1 .. 7
    Dim EdTimeSet As Bit                // 1 = the clock screen's date or time changed: OK sets the DS1307
    ScrMode = SCR_MAIN
    ScrTurn = LANDSCAPE
    LogRun = LOG_AT_START               // LOG_ON or LOG_OFF, from the settings

    LinesWritten = 0
    LinesLost = 0
    TickCount = 0
    Sample = 0                          // shown as 0 until the first sample
    TapCount = 0

    // The screen (InitGLCD has run, from glcd.h's #startup)
    ScreenFrame
    ScreenStatus("Starting", SCR_TEXT)

    // Prevents the terminal becoming active too early, during reprogramming
    Wait 2 s
    ConsoleCRLF()
    ConsoleText("RTCLOG.CSV: ") : ConsoleText(SAMPLE_LABEL) : ConsoleText(", ")
    ConsoleText("ATmega328P")
    ConsoleCRLF()

    // ----- The clock: there, and running? (each I2C transfer resets the display: the screen is started again after)
    // SDA and SCL inputs first: InitGLCD left SDA (A4, the display's RESET) a driven output
    Dir HI2C_DATA In
    Dir HI2C_CLOCK In
    If ClockFound() = 0 Then            // (it starts the TWI too)
        // where the date and the time go on the main screen (ScreenClock: LogLine's characters 1 .. 10 and 12 .. 19)
        LogLine = "No DS1307 ,No clock"
        ScreenStart
            
        Do
        Loop
    End If
    DriftStart                          // the drift and its total from the DS1307's RAM
    ClockOK = ClockRunning()
    ClockRead
    ScreenStart
    // the time can be sent for SET_WAIT seconds (T yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss); a stopped clock not set then opens the
    // clock screen
    ConsoleText("   Time ") : ConsoleLine(LogLine)
    If ClockOK = 1 Then
        ScreenStatus("Send T yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss", SCR_TEXT)
    Else
        ScreenStatus("Clock stopped: send T yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss", SCR_BAD)
    End If
    ConsoleLine("   Send T")
    If ClockSet(SET_WAIT) = 0 Then
        If ClockOK = 0 Then ClockScrOpen
    End If

    // ----- The time from here on: Timer1, once a second, and the DS1307 once an hour
    ClockRead                           // the DS1307's time now
    ScreenStart
    TickStart

    // ----- Logging
    LogReady = 0
    LogLost = 0
    Do
        // each second from Timer1: the time on, and on the screen; a sample when the seconds are a multiple of
        // LOG_EVERY. Seconds missed while the card or the screen was busy are caught up here, one at a time.
        Do
            ScreenTouch                 // a tap: the menu, a button, or back from black
        Loop While TickCount = 0
        IntOff
        TickCount--
        IntOn
        ClockAddSecond
        ClockLine                       // LogLine = "yyyy-mm-dd,hh:mm:ss"
        ScreenClock
        If ScrMode = SCR_SETCLOCK Then ClockScrTick     // the clock screen's time runs on too
        // the menu goes after MENU_WAIT seconds with no tap, the clock screen after CLOCK_WAIT (both odd)
        If ScrMode.0 = 1 Then
            MenuSecs--
            If MenuSecs = 0 Then ScreenMain
        End If

        // once an hour, at hh:00:30: the drift, then the DS1307's time again (each I2C transfer resets the display:
        // ScreenStart draws it again). At 30 s a second moved for the drift does not change the minute
        If RTCMin = 0 And RTCSec = 30 Then
            DriftHour
            ClockRead
            TickStart
            ScreenStart
            ConsoleText("   Time ") : ConsoleLine(LogLine)
        End If

        If RTCSec % LOG_EVERY <> 0 Then Goto NextSecond
        // the sample is taken and shown while not logging too; it is written only while logging
        Sample = ChipTemp()
        LogLine = LogLine + "," + Str(Sample)
        ConsoleText(LogLine)
        If LogRun = 1 Then
            // Write the line. A failure (eg the card pulled out) closes the drive
            If LogReady = 1 Then
                If LogWrite() = 0 Then LogReady = 0
            End If
            // No drive, at the start or after a failure: start it again (a card put back is found here)
            // and write the line, so a card put back between two samples loses no sample
            If LogReady = 0 Then
                LogReady = LogStart()
                If LogReady = 1 Then
                    If LogWrite() = 0 Then LogReady = 0
                End If
            End If
            If LogReady = 1 Then
                ConsoleText("  written")
                LinesWritten++
                ScreenStatus("RTCLOG.CSV: written", SCR_GOOD)
            Else
                ConsoleText("   No card ")
                LogLost = 1                 // a "Restarted" line before the next line written
                LinesLost++
                ScreenStatus("   No card ", SCR_BAD)
            End If
        End If
        ConsoleCRLF()
        ScreenSample
NextSecond:
    Loop

// ----- The screen

'''Start the display again (after an I2C transfer has reset it) and draw what is up: the main screen, the menu,
'''or black
Sub ScreenStart
    InitGLCD
    If ScrMode = SCR_MAIN Then ScreenDraw
    If ScrMode = SCR_MENU Then MenuDraw
    If ScrMode = SCR_BLACK Then GLCDCLS SCR_BACK
    If ScrMode = SCR_SETCLOCK Then ClockScrDraw
End Sub

'''The touch panel, read every 20 ms while waiting for the next second. On the main screen a tap shows the menu;
'''on the menu a tap is a button (or the title: back); on the black screen a tap is back to the main screen; on
'''the clock screen a tap is one of its buttons (ClockScrTouch).
Sub ScreenTouch
    Dim MenuButton As Byte
    If TouchEvent() = 1 Then
        MenuButton = MenuPressed()      // where it was pressed (still pressed): the log, and the menu's button
        TouchLog(MenuButton)
        If ScrMode = SCR_SETCLOCK Then
            ClockScrTouch
            Goto TouchDone
        End If
        If ScrMode = SCR_MAIN Then
            ScrMode = SCR_MENU
            MenuSecs = MENU_WAIT
            MenuDraw
        Else
            If ScrMode = SCR_BLACK Then
                // the display started again (InitGLCD, then the main screen), whatever state the panel is in
                ScrMode = SCR_MAIN
                ScreenStart
            Else
                // the menu: the button, from MenuPressed above
                If MenuButton = 1 Then
                    If LogRun = 1 Then
                        LogRun = 0
                        ConsoleLine("   Not logging")
                    Else
                        LogRun = 1
                        ConsoleLine("   Logging")
                    End If
                End If
                If MenuButton = 2 Then
                    If ScrTurn = LANDSCAPE Then
                        ScrTurn = LANDSCAPE_REV
                    Else
                        ScrTurn = LANDSCAPE
                    End If
                End If
                If MenuButton = 3 Then
                    ScrMode = SCR_BLACK
                    GLCDCLS SCR_BACK
                Else
                    If MenuButton = 4 Then
                        ClockScrOpen
                    Else
                        ScreenMain          // buttons 1 and 2, and the title (0): back to the main screen
                    End If
                End If
            End If
        End If
    End If
TouchDone:
    Wait 20 ms
End Sub

'''Back to the main screen, all of it drawn
Sub ScreenMain
    ScrMode = SCR_MAIN
    ScreenDraw
End Sub

'''All of the main screen, drawn again (ScreenFrame sets the way round)
Sub ScreenDraw
    ScreenFrame
    ScreenClock
    ScreenSample
    If LogRun = 0 Then ScreenStatus("   Not logging", SCR_BAD)
End Sub

'''The menu: a title and four buttons across the screen, y 30 .. 77, 84 .. 131, 138 .. 185 and 192 .. 239
Sub MenuDraw
    Dim MenuY As Word
    ScreenBlank
    GLCDPrint(4, 6, "Menu", SCR_TITLE)
    MenuY = 30
    Repeat 4
        ScreenBox(0, MenuY, 319, MenuY + 47, SCR_BUTTON)
        MenuY += 54
    End Repeat
    GLCDBackground = SCR_BUTTON         // the letters' background: the button
    If LogRun = 1 Then
        GLCDPrint(20, 47, "1  Stop logging", SCR_CLOCK)
    Else
        GLCDPrint(20, 47, "1  Start logging", SCR_CLOCK)
    End If
    GLCDPrint(20, 101, "2  Rotate screen", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDPrint(20, 155, "3  Black screen", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDPrint(20, 208, "4  Set clock", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDBackground = SCR_BACK
End Sub

'''The menu button pressed: 1 .. 4 (0 = the title), from where the panel is pressed up and down the screen: the
'''panel's raw X (TouchRaw, for the log; MenuRaw, the same the screen's way up) against TOUCH_RAW_B1 .. B4 (the
'''button edges, worked out from the calibration when compiling: no 32-bit sums here)
Function MenuPressed As Byte
    // both readings now, while the panel is pressed: the tap's log (the console, at 9600 baud) comes before the
    // clock screen looks at it, and by then the finger is often off (an open panel reads high: always "<")
    TouchRaw = TouchRawX()
    ClkRaw = TouchRawY()
    MenuRaw = TouchRaw
    If ScrTurn <> LANDSCAPE Then
        // turned round: screen y is 239 - y, the raw X the other way from TOUCH_RAW_YSUM (0 past it: the top)
        MenuRaw = 0
        If TouchRaw < TOUCH_RAW_YSUM Then MenuRaw = TOUCH_RAW_YSUM - TouchRaw
    End If
    MenuPressed = 0
    If MenuRaw >= TOUCH_RAW_B1 Then MenuPressed = 1
    If MenuRaw >= TOUCH_RAW_B2 Then MenuPressed = 2
    If MenuRaw >= TOUCH_RAW_B3 Then MenuPressed = 3
    If MenuRaw >= TOUCH_RAW_B4 Then MenuPressed = 4
End Function

// ----- The clock screen

'''Open the clock screen (the menu's button 4): the DS1307's time and the drift to change, the year first
Sub ClockScrOpen
    EdVal(1) = RTCYear
    EdVal(2) = RTCMonth
    EdVal(3) = RTCDay
    EdVal(4) = RTCHour
    EdVal(5) = RTCMin
    EdVal(6) = RTCSec
    EdDrift = ClockDrift
    EdField = 1
    EdTimeSet = 0
    ScrMode = SCR_SETCLOCK
    MenuSecs = CLOCK_WAIT
    ClockScrDraw
End Sub

'''The clock screen: a title, what does not change in the three rows (the values go in its gaps), the values
'''(ClockScrValues), and six buttons along the foot (from y 172): < > - + OK X, drawn as one bar and one line of
'''labels, then five black gaps between the buttons (fewer calls: less flash)
Sub ClockScrDraw
    Dim ClkX As Word
    ScreenBlank
    GLCDPrint(4, 6, "Set clock", SCR_TITLE)
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 3              // 18 pixels a character
    GLCDPrint(20, 40, "20  -  -", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDPrint(56, 84, ":  :", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDPrint(20, 128, "Drift      ppm", SCR_CLOCK)
    ScreenBox(0, 172, 319, 239, SCR_BUTTON)
    GLCDBackground = SCR_BUTTON
    GLCDPrint(17, 194, "<  >  -  + OK  X", SCR_CLOCK)
    GLCDBackground = SCR_BACK
    ClkX = 52
    Repeat 5
        ScreenBox(ClkX, 172, ClkX + 2, 239, SCR_BACK)
        ClkX += 53
    End Repeat
    ClockScrValues
End Sub

'''One second on for the clock screen's time, so OK sets the time as it is then, not as it was when the screen
'''opened: the seconds, the minutes and the hours carry on, each drawn again as it changes (fixed elements: less
'''flash than a loop). The hour goes from 23 to 0 without the date on (the screen open across midnight: set the date)
Sub ClockScrTick
    EdVal(6)++
    If EdVal(6) = 60 Then
        EdVal(6) = 0
        EdVal(5)++
        If EdVal(5) = 60 Then
            EdVal(5) = 0
            EdVal(4)++
            If EdVal(4) = 24 Then EdVal(4) = 0
            ClockScrField(4)
        End If
        ClockScrField(5)
    End If
    ClockScrField(6)
End Sub

'''The clock screen's seven values (ClockScrField)
Sub ClockScrValues
    Dim ClkI As Byte
    For ClkI = 1 To 7
        ClockScrField(ClkI)
    Next
End Sub

'''One of the clock screen's values, at its place from ClockFieldX and ClockFieldY, digit by digit, and a bar under
'''it: lit when it is the field being changed, black when not. The drift: its sign, then three digits. One field
'''at a time after a tap: drawing them all (a pixel at a time, at size 3) took long enough to miss taps
Sub ClockScrField(In ClkI)
    Dim ClkV, ClkY, ClkW, ClkC As Byte
    Dim ClkX, ClkBar As Word
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 3
        ReadTable ClockFieldX, ClkI, ClkX
        ReadTable ClockFieldY, ClkI, ClkY
        ClkV = EdVal(ClkI)
        ClkW = 35
        If ClkI = 7 Then
            ClkW = 53
            ClkC = 43                   // +
            ClkV = EdDrift              // the low byte: ppm + 256 is 0x01pp from 0 up, 0x00nn below (256 - ppm)
            If EdDrift_H = 0 Then
                ClkC = 45               // -
                ClkV = 0 - ClkV
            End If
            GLCDDrawChar(ClkX, ClkY, ClkC, SCR_CLOCK)
            ClkX += 18
        End If
        ClkBar = SCR_BACK
        If ClkI = EdField Then ClkBar = SCR_TEXT
        ScreenBox(ClkX, ClkY + 24, ClkX + ClkW, ClkY + 26, ClkBar)
        If ClkI = 7 Then
            GLCDDrawChar(ClkX, ClkY, 48 + ClkV / 100, SCR_CLOCK)
            ClkV = ClkV % 100
            ClkX += 18
        End If
        GLCDDrawChar(ClkX, ClkY, 48 + ClkV / 10, SCR_CLOCK)
        GLCDDrawChar(ClkX + 18, ClkY, 48 + ClkV % 10, SCR_CLOCK)
End Sub

// where each field starts: yy, mm, dd (after "20", from x 20, 18 pixels a character), hh, mm, ss, the drift's sign
// (after "Drift ")
Table ClockFieldX
    56
    110
    164
    20
    74
    128
    128
End Table

Table ClockFieldY
    40
    40
    40
    84
    84
    84
    128
End Table

// each field's lowest and highest value: year 00 .. 99, month, day (the month's length is checked when set),
// hour, minute, second (the drift: ClockStep, -250 .. 250)
Table ClockFieldMin
    0
    1
    1
    0
    0
    0
End Table

Table ClockFieldMax
    99
    12
    31
    23
    59
    59
End Table

'''A tap on the clock screen: one of the six buttons along the foot (anywhere else does nothing). Which button is
'''from the panel's raw Y (across the screen) against TOUCH_RAW_E1 .. E5; turned round, the buttons are the other
'''way
Sub ClockScrTouch
    Dim ClkBtn, ClkOld, ClkHeld As Byte
    // the row of buttons (MenuRaw: up and down the screen, the screen's way up, from MenuPressed)
    If MenuRaw < TOUCH_RAW_ROW Then Exit Sub
    ClkBtn = 1                              // ClkRaw: across the screen, from MenuPressed
    If ClkRaw <= TOUCH_RAW_E1 Then ClkBtn = 2
    If ClkRaw <= TOUCH_RAW_E2 Then ClkBtn = 3
    If ClkRaw <= TOUCH_RAW_E3 Then ClkBtn = 4
    If ClkRaw <= TOUCH_RAW_E4 Then ClkBtn = 5
    If ClkRaw <= TOUCH_RAW_E5 Then ClkBtn = 6
    If ScrTurn <> LANDSCAPE Then ClkBtn = 7 - ClkBtn
    MenuSecs = CLOCK_WAIT                   // a tap: the time-out starts again
    If ClkBtn = 6 Then                      // X: no change
        ScreenMain
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If ClkBtn = 5 Then                      // OK: the drift, then the DS1307 set
        If EdDrift <> ClockDrift Then
            ClockDrift = EdDrift
            DriftTotal = 0                  // a new drift: none built up yet
            DriftSave
        End If
        ScrMode = SCR_MAIN
        If EdTimeSet = 0 Then               // the date and time not changed: the clock runs on as it is
            ScreenStart                     // InitGLCD too: the I2C (DriftSave) upsets the display
            Exit Sub
        End If
        If ClockStore() = 1 Then
            TickStart
        Else
            ScrMode = SCR_SETCLOCK          // a value out of range (from a stopped clock): the clock screen stays
        End If
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If ClkBtn < 3 Then
        ClkOld = EdField
        If ClkBtn = 1 Then                  // <: the field before
            EdField--
            If EdField = 0 Then EdField = 7
        Else                                // >: the next field
            EdField++
            If EdField = 8 Then EdField = 1
        End If
        ClockScrField(ClkOld)               // its bar off, the new field's on
        ClockScrField(EdField)
        Exit Sub
    End If
    // - and +: one step; held for half a second, steps of 10, about 3 a second while it is held
    ClockStep(ClkBtn)
    ClockScrField(EdField)
    ClkHeld = 0
    Do While TouchPressed() = 1
        Wait 10 ms
        ClkHeld++
        If ClkHeld >= 50 Then
            Repeat 10
                ClockStep(ClkBtn)
            End Repeat
            ClockScrField(EdField)
            ClkHeld = 20                    // the next in 0.3 s and the drawing
        End If
    Loop
    MenuSecs = CLOCK_WAIT
End Sub

'''The field being changed one down (StepBtn 3, -) or up (4, +): the date and time round from one end to the other,
'''the drift stops at -250 and 250
Sub ClockStep(In StepBtn)
    Dim StepV, StepLow, StepHigh As Byte
    If EdField = 7 Then
        If StepBtn = 3 Then
            If EdDrift > 6 Then EdDrift--
        Else
            If EdDrift < 506 Then EdDrift++
        End If
        Exit Sub
    End If
    StepV = EdVal(EdField)
    ReadTable ClockFieldMin, EdField, StepLow
    ReadTable ClockFieldMax, EdField, StepHigh
    If StepBtn = 3 Then
        If StepV > StepLow Then
            StepV--
        Else
            StepV = StepHigh
        End If
    Else
        If StepV < StepHigh Then
            StepV++
        Else
            StepV = StepLow
        End If
    End If
    EdVal(EdField) = StepV
    EdTimeSet = 1
End Sub

// ----- The drift

'''The drift and its running total from the DS1307's RAM; CLOCK_DRIFT and 0 when they are not there (a new DS1307,
'''or its battery taken out)
Sub DriftStart
    DsRead(DS_RAM_MARK, 5)              // the mark, the drift (low, high), the total (low, high)
    If DsBuf(1) = DS_MARK Then
        ClockDrift = DsBuf(2)
        ClockDrift_H = DsBuf(3)
        DriftTotal = DsBuf(4)
        DriftTotal_H = DsBuf(5)
    Else
        ClockDrift = CLOCK_DRIFT_B
        DriftTotal = 0
        DriftSave
    End If
End Sub

'''The mark, the drift and its running total to the DS1307's RAM
Sub DriftSave
    DsBuf(1) = DS_MARK
    DsBuf(2) = ClockDrift
    DsBuf(3) = ClockDrift_H
    DsBuf(4) = DriftTotal
    DsBuf(5) = DriftTotal_H
    DsWrite(DS_RAM_MARK, 5)
End Sub

'''Once an hour (at hh:00:30): an hour's drift added to the total, 36 x ppm in 0.1 ms (3600 s x ppm / 1000000 s,
'''in 0.0001 s). Each whole second (10000) moves the DS1307's seconds one back (it gains) or on (it loses)
Sub DriftHour
    Dim DriftStep As Word
    Dim DriftPpm As Byte
    DriftPpm = ClockDrift               // the size, as in ClockScrField: the low byte, negated below 256
    If ClockDrift_H = 0 Then DriftPpm = 0 - DriftPpm
    DriftStep = DriftPpm
    DriftStep = DriftStep * 36
    DriftTotal = DriftTotal + DriftStep
    If DriftTotal >= 10000 Then
        DriftTotal = DriftTotal - 10000
        DsRead(0, 1)
        DriftPpm = BcdToDec(DsBuf(1) And 0x7F)  // the seconds (at 30: no carry either way)
        If ClockDrift_H = 1 Then        // + (a whole second built up: not 0 ppm)
            DriftPpm--
        Else
            DriftPpm++
        End If
        DsBuf(1) = DecToBcd(DriftPpm)       // bit 7 (CH) clear: the clock runs on
        DsWrite(0, 1)
        ConsoleLine("   Drift: 1 s")
    End If
    DriftSave
End Sub

'''A blank screen, the way round it is set to, and the font at size 2: the main screen, the menu, the clock screen
Sub ScreenBlank
    GLCDRotate(ScrTurn)
    GLCDBackground = SCR_BACK
    GLCDCLS SCR_BACK
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 2
End Sub

'''The title, the rules and the labels that do not change
Sub ScreenFrame
    ScreenBlank
    GLCDPrint(4, 4, "GCBASIC data logger", SCR_TITLE)
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 1
    GLCDPrint(4, 24, "ATmega328P, SD card, DS1307", SCR_TITLE)
    // the rules: boxes, as GLCDLine runs the compiler out of registers on the ATmega328P (build 1673)
    ScreenBox(0, 36, 319, 37, SCR_TITLE)
    ScreenBox(0, 140, 319, 141, SCR_TITLE)
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 2
    GLCDPrint(4, 150, SAMPLE_LABEL, SCR_TEXT)
    GLCDPrint(4, 174, "Written", SCR_TEXT)
    GLCDPrint(4, 198, "Lost", SCR_TEXT)
End Sub

'''The date and time (from LogLine, "yyyy-mm-dd,hh:mm:ss"): the time large, the date under it
Sub ScreenClock
    Dim ScrTime As String * 8
    Dim ScrDate As String * 10
    If ScrMode <> SCR_MAIN Then Exit Sub    // the menu or black is up
    Dim ScrI As Byte
    // LogLine's characters 1 .. 10 and 12 .. 19 (a string is its length, element 0, then its characters)
    For ScrI = 1 To 10
        ScrDate(ScrI) = LogLine(ScrI)
    Next
    ScrDate(0) = 10
    For ScrI = 1 To 8
        ScrTime(ScrI) = LogLine(ScrI + 11)
    Next
    ScrTime(0) = 8
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 5
    GLCDPrint(40, 50, ScrTime, SCR_CLOCK)       // 8 x 30 = 240 pixels wide, 40 high
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 2
    GLCDPrint(100, 108, ScrDate, SCR_CLOCK)
End Sub

'''The last sample, and the lines written and lost
Sub ScreenSample
    Dim ScrValue As String * 10
    If ScrMode <> SCR_MAIN Then Exit Sub    // the menu or black is up
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 2
    ScrValue = Str(Sample) + SAMPLE_UNIT        // spaces clear what a longer value left
    GLCDPrint(136, 150, ScrValue, SCR_CLOCK)
    ScrValue = Str(LinesWritten) + "    "
    GLCDPrint(136, 174, ScrValue, SCR_GOOD)
    ScrValue = Str(LinesLost) + "    "
    GLCDPrint(136, 198, ScrValue, SCR_BAD)
End Sub

'''A box filled with a colour, from x1, y1 to x2, y2 (x1 <= x2, y1 <= y2): glcd_ili9341.h's FilledBox without the
'''corners put in order, and without its 32-bit pixel count (one line at a time instead): less flash, as fast
Sub ScreenBox(In BoxX1 As Word, In BoxY1 As Word, In BoxX2 As Word, In BoxY2 As Word, In BoxColour As Word)
    Dim BoxWide, BoxHigh As Word
    SetAddressWindow_ILI9341(BoxX1, BoxY1, BoxX2, BoxY2)
    BoxWide = BoxX2 - BoxX1 + 1
    BoxHigh = BoxY2 - BoxY1 + 1
    Repeat BoxHigh
        Repeat BoxWide
            SendWord_ILI9341(BoxColour)
        End Repeat
    End Repeat
End Sub

'''The status line at the foot of the screen, in a colour (the rest of the line cleared)
Sub ScreenStatus(In ScrText As String, In ScrColour As Word)
    If ScrMode <> SCR_MAIN Then Exit Sub    // the menu or black is up
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 1
    ScreenBox(4, 226, 319, 235, SCR_BACK)
    GLCDPrint(4, 226, ScrText, ScrColour)
End Sub

// ----- The display's start

'''The display started: glcd_ili9341.h's InitGLCD_ILI9341 for this shield (the 8-bit bus), its 70 setting bytes
'''from a table instead of a call each (about 360 words less flash). The #define InitGLCD_ILI9341 ScreenInit at the
'''top has the compiler's start-up call this in place of the library's
Sub ScreenInit
    Dim InitAt, InitCount, InitByte As Byte
    Dir ILI9341_DB7 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB6 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB5 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB4 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB3 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB2 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB1 Out
    Dir ILI9341_DB0 Out
    Dir ILI9341_RD Out
    Dir ILI9341_WR Out
    Dir ILI9341_RS Out
    Dir ILI9341_CS Out
    Dir ILI9341_RST Out
    Set ILI9341_RD On
    Set ILI9341_WR On
    Set ILI9341_RS On
    Set ILI9341_CS On
    Set ILI9341_RST On
    // reset: low for at least 10 us
    Wait 65 ms
    Set ILI9341_RST Off
    Wait 15 us
    Set ILI9341_RST On
    Wait 15 ms
    // each entry: how many data bytes, the command, its data; 255 at the end
    InitAt = 1
    Do
        ReadTable ScreenInitData, InitAt, InitCount
        If InitCount = 255 Then Exit Do
        InitAt++
        ReadTable ScreenInitData, InitAt, InitByte
        SendCommand_ILI9341(InitByte)
        Repeat InitCount
            InitAt++
            ReadTable ScreenInitData, InitAt, InitByte
            SendData_ILI9341(InitByte)
        End Repeat
        InitAt++
    Loop
    SendCommand_ILI9341(ILI9341_SLPOUT)     // out of sleep
    Wait 150 ms
    SendCommand_ILI9341(ILI9341_DISPON)     // display on
    // what the library sets up for the drawing routines
    GLCDBACKGROUND = ILI9341_BLACK
    GLCDForeground = ILI9341_WHITE
    ILI9341_GLCD_WIDTH = GLCD_WIDTH
    ILI9341_GLCD_HEIGHT = GLCD_HEIGHT
    GLCDFontWidth = 6
    GLCDfntDefault = 0
    GLCDfntDefaultsize = 1
    GLCDfntDefaultHeight = 7
    GLCDRotateState = Portrait
    GLCDCLS
    SendCommand_ILI9341(ILI9341_DISPON)
End Sub

// the ILI9341's settings, as glcd_ili9341.h sends them: the number of data bytes, the command, the data
Table ScreenInitData
    3, 0xEF, 0x03, 0x80, 0x02
    3, 0xCF, 0x00, 0xC1, 0x30
    4, 0xED, 0x64, 0x03, 0x12, 0x81
    3, 0xE8, 0x85, 0x00, 0x78
    5, 0xCB, 0x39, 0x2C, 0x00, 0x34, 0x02
    1, 0xF7, 0x20
    2, 0xEA, 0x00, 0x00
    1, 0xC0, 0x2B
    1, 0xC1, 0x10
    2, 0xC5, 0x3E, 0x28
    1, 0xC7, 0x86
    1, 0x36, 0x48
    1, 0x3A, 0x55
    2, 0xB1, 0x00, 0x18
    3, 0xB6, 0x08, 0x82, 0x27
    1, 0xF2, 0x00
    1, 0x26, 0x01
    15, 0xE0, 0x0F, 0x31, 0x2B, 0x0C, 0x0E, 0x08, 0x4E, 0xF1, 0x37, 0x07, 0x10, 0x03, 0x0E, 0x09, 0x00
    15, 0xE1, 0x00, 0x0E, 0x14, 0x03, 0x11, 0x07, 0x31, 0xC1, 0x48, 0x08, 0x0F, 0x0C, 0x31, 0x36, 0x0F
    255
End Table

// ----- The chip temperature

'''The ATmega328P's temperature sensor (ADC channel 8, 1.1 V internal reference), in whole C (0 below 0 C).
'''Not calibrated: TEMP_OFFSET is the reading at 0 C.
Function ChipTemp As Byte
    Dim TempRaw As Word
    ADMUX = 0xC8                        // REFS1:0 = 11, the 1.1 V reference; MUX = 1000, the temperature sensor
    ADCSRA = 0x87                       // ADEN, clock / 128 (125 kHz)
    // the reference settles: the touch panel's reading (ReadAD10) leaves the ADC on AVcc (5 V), and the Uno's 100 nF
    // on AREF takes a few tens of ms to come down to 1.1 V. Too short a wait reads low (0 C)
    Wait 40 ms
    Repeat 2                            // the first conversion after a change is thrown away
        Set ADCSRA.ADSC On
        Wait While ADCSRA.ADSC = On
    End Repeat
    [Byte]TempRaw = ADCL                // ADCL first: it locks ADCH
    TempRaw_H = ADCH
    ChipTemp = 0
    If TempRaw > TEMP_OFFSET Then ChipTemp = TempRaw - TEMP_OFFSET
End Function

// ----- The clock

'''1 when the DS1307 answers on the I2C. The ds1307.h routines wait for an answer for ever, so this is asked first.
Function ClockFound As Byte
    ClockFound = 0
    // the bus's pull-ups first (on the DS1307's board): SDA and SCL held low, then let go, rise at once with them.
    // With none (the board off) they stay low, and the TWI's start would wait for ever (a white screen)
    HI2C_DATA = 0
    HI2C_CLOCK = 0
    Dir HI2C_DATA Out
    Dir HI2C_CLOCK Out
    Dir HI2C_DATA In
    Dir HI2C_CLOCK In
    Wait 20 us
    If HI2C_DATA = 0 Then Exit Function
    If HI2C_CLOCK = 0 Then Exit Function
    HI2CMode Master                     // the TWI as master at HI2C_BAUD_RATE (the AVR needs this before any I2C)
    HI2CReStart
    HI2CSend(DS_AddrWrite)
    HI2CStop
    If HI2CAckPollState = False Then ClockFound = 1
End Function

'''1 when the DS1307's oscillator runs (the CH bit, bit 7 of register 0, is clear) in 24-hour mode (bit 6 of
'''register 2 clear: ClockStore sets it so). 0 has the time set again
Function ClockRunning As Byte
    DsRead(0, 3)
    ClockRunning = 1
    If DsBuf(1).7 = 1 Then ClockRunning = 0
    If DsBuf(3).6 = 1 Then ClockRunning = 0
End Function

'''Read the date and time from the DS1307 into RTCDay ... RTCSec, and LogLine = "yyyy-mm-dd,hh:mm:ss".
'''An I2C transfer: it resets the display (A4), so call ScreenStart after it.
Sub ClockRead
    DsRead(0, 7)
    RTCSec = BcdToDec(DsBuf(1) And 0x7F)    // bit 7: CH
    RTCMin = BcdToDec(DsBuf(2))
    RTCHour = BcdToDec(DsBuf(3) And 0x3F)   // 24-hour mode
    RTCDay = BcdToDec(DsBuf(5))             // register 3 is the day of the week
    RTCMonth = BcdToDec(DsBuf(6))
    RTCYear = BcdToDec(DsBuf(7))
    ClockLine
End Sub

'''Read DsCount (1 .. 7) of the DS1307's registers, from DsAddr, into DsBuf(1) on. The ds1307.h routines each
'''read or write the registers their own way: these two, for all of them, take less flash
Sub DsRead(In DsAddr, In DsCount)
    Dim DsI, DsByte As Byte
    HI2CReStart
    HI2CSend(DS_AddrWrite)
    HI2CSend(DsAddr)
    HI2CReStart
    HI2CSend(DS_AddrRead)
    For DsI = 1 To DsCount
        If DsI = DsCount Then
            HI2CReceive(DsByte, NACK)       // the last: no ACK
        Else
            HI2CReceive(DsByte)
        End If
        DsBuf(DsI) = DsByte
    Next
    HI2CStop
End Sub

'''Write DsBuf(1) on to DsCount (1 .. 7) of the DS1307's registers, from DsAddr
Sub DsWrite(In DsAddr, In DsCount)
    Dim DsI As Byte
    HI2CReStart
    HI2CSend(DS_AddrWrite)
    HI2CSend(DsAddr)
    For DsI = 1 To DsCount
        HI2CSend(DsBuf(DsI))
    Next
    HI2CStop
End Sub

'''LogLine = "yyyy-mm-dd,hh:mm:ss" from RTCYear ... RTCSec
Sub ClockLine
    LogLine = "20"
    AddTwo(RTCYear, 45)                 // -
    AddTwo(RTCMonth, 45)
    AddTwo(RTCDay, 44)                  // ,
    AddTwo(RTCHour, 58)                 // :
    AddTwo(RTCMin, 58)
    AddTwo(RTCSec, 0)
End Sub

'''Timer1 from 0: compare match A (TICK_TOP) once a second, CTC mode, the clock divided by TICK_CLOCK's
'''prescaler, its interrupt on
Sub TickStart
    IntOff
    TCCR1A = 0
    TCCR1B = 0                          // stopped while it is set
    TCNT1H = 0                          // 16-bit registers: the high byte first
    TCNT1L = 0
    OCR1AH = TICK_TOP / 256
    OCR1AL = TICK_TOP And 255
    TickCount = 0
    TCCR1B = TICK_CLOCK                 // CTC, to OCR1A, and the prescaler: see TICK_TOP
    On Interrupt Timer1Match1 Call ClockTick
    IntOn
End Sub

'''Timer1's interrupt, once a second: count it, the main program adds it to the time
Sub ClockTick
    TickCount++
End Sub

'''One second on: the seconds, minutes, hours, and at midnight the date (month lengths, leap years 2000 .. 2099)
Sub ClockAddSecond
    Dim DaysInMonth As Byte
    RTCSec++
    If RTCSec < 60 Then Exit Sub
    RTCSec = 0
    RTCMin++
    If RTCMin < 60 Then Exit Sub
    RTCMin = 0
    RTCHour++
    If RTCHour < 24 Then Exit Sub
    RTCHour = 0
    RTCDay++
    ReadTable MonthDays, RTCMonth, DaysInMonth
    If RTCMonth = 2 Then
        If RTCYear % 4 = 0 Then DaysInMonth = 29         // 2000 .. 2099: every fourth year
    End If
    If RTCDay <= DaysInMonth Then Exit Sub
    RTCDay = 1
    RTCMonth++
    If RTCMonth <= 12 Then Exit Sub
    RTCMonth = 1
    RTCYear++
End Sub

Table MonthDays
    31
    28
    31
    30
    31
    30
    31
    31
    30
    31
    30
    31
End Table

'''FatDate and FatTime (FAT format) from the DS1307's date and time: the date and time FatCommit writes
'''into the file's entry in the folder. Set before each FatCommit: FatMount sets them to 2026-01-01.
Sub ClockToFat
    FatDate = (RTCYear + 20) * 512 + RTCMonth * 32 + RTCDay       // years from 1980, month, day
    FatTime = RTCHour * 2048 + RTCMin * 32 + RTCSec / 2           // hours, minutes, 2-second steps
End Sub

'''Add a number 0 .. 99 to LogLine as two digits, then the character TwoSep (0: none)
Sub AddTwo(In TwoValue, In TwoSep)
    Dim TwoLen As Byte
    // the string is its length (element 0) and the characters: add them at the end
    TwoLen = LogLine(0)
    LogLine(TwoLen + 1) = 48 + TwoValue / 10
    LogLine(TwoLen + 2) = 48 + TwoValue % 10
    TwoLen += 2
    If TwoSep <> 0 Then
        TwoLen++
        LogLine(TwoLen) = TwoSep
    End If
    LogLine(0) = TwoLen
End Sub

'''Wait for "T" and the time on the serial port, then set the DS1307: 14 digits yyyymmddhhmmss, any separators,
'''ending with CR or LF. SetSecs: how long to wait (0: until a good time comes). Returns 1 when the clock was set.
Function ClockSet(In SetSecs) As Byte
    Dim SetChar, SetCount As Byte
    Dim SetDigits(14) As Byte
    Dim SetTaking As Bit
    Dim SetWait As Word

    Dim SetLimit As Word

    ClockSet = 0
    SetTaking = 0
    SetCount = 0
    SetWait = 0
    SetLimit = SetSecs * 1000           // in 1 ms steps
    Do
        If USARTHasData Then
            SetChar = HSerReceiveFrom(1)
            If SetChar = 84 Or SetChar = 116 Then           // T or t: the start
                SetTaking = 1
                SetCount = 0
            End If
            If SetChar = 13 Or SetChar = 10 Then            // CR or LF: the end
                If SetTaking = 1 Then Exit Do
            End If
            If SetChar >= 48 And SetChar <= 57 Then         // a digit
                If SetTaking = 1 And SetCount < 14 Then
                    SetCount++
                    SetDigits(SetCount) = SetChar - 48
                End If
            End If
        Else
            Wait 1 ms
            If SetSecs > 0 Then
                SetWait++
                If SetWait >= SetLimit Then Exit Function
            End If
        End If
    Loop

    // 14 digits: yyyy mm dd hh mm ss, 2000 .. 2099
    If SetCount <> 14 Or SetDigits(1) <> 2 Or SetDigits(2) <> 0 Then
        ConsoleLine("   Bad time")
        Exit Function
    End If
    EdVal(1) = SetDigits(3) * 10 + SetDigits(4)
    EdVal(2) = SetDigits(5) * 10 + SetDigits(6)
    EdVal(3) = SetDigits(7) * 10 + SetDigits(8)
    EdVal(4) = SetDigits(9) * 10 + SetDigits(10)
    EdVal(5) = SetDigits(11) * 10 + SetDigits(12)
    EdVal(6) = SetDigits(13) * 10 + SetDigits(14)
    ClockSet = ClockStore()
End Function

'''Set the DS1307 from EdVal(1) .. EdVal(6) (year 00 .. 99, month, day, hour, minute, second: from the serial T line,
'''or the clock screen): checks the values (a day past the month's end is its last day), works out the day of the
'''week, and starts the clock. Then the time again from the DS1307, and the screen started again (the I2C transfers
'''reset it). Returns 1 when set, 0 (and "Bad time") when a value is out of range
Function ClockStore As Byte
    Dim StDow, StDays, StYear As Byte
    ClockStore = 0
    // each value in range (the clock screen's limits)
    For StYear = 1 To 6
        ReadTable ClockFieldMin, StYear, StDow
        ReadTable ClockFieldMax, StYear, StDays
        If EdVal(StYear) < StDow Or EdVal(StYear) > StDays Then
            ConsoleLine("   Bad time")
            Exit Function
        End If
    Next
    ReadTable MonthDays, EdVal(2), StDays
    If EdVal(2) = 2 Then
        If EdVal(1) % 4 = 0 Then StDays = 29    // 2000 .. 2099: every fourth year
    End If
    If EdVal(3) > StDays Then EdVal(3) = StDays

    // the day of the week, 1 = Sunday (as the ds1307.h demonstration): Sakamoto's method. For 2000 + y the
    // century's terms come to whole weeks, so y + y / 4 is enough; and 28 years on is the same day (28 + 7 days),
    // so y + 28 keeps January and February 2000 (counted in the year before) in a byte
    StYear = EdVal(1) + 28
    If EdVal(2) < 3 Then StYear--
    StDow = (StYear + StYear / 4 + MonthKey(EdVal(2)) + EdVal(3)) % 7 + 1

    DsBuf(1) = DecToBcd(EdVal(6))       // bit 7 (CH) clear: the clock runs
    DsBuf(2) = DecToBcd(EdVal(5))
    DsBuf(3) = DecToBcd(EdVal(4))       // bit 6 clear: 24-hour mode
    DsBuf(4) = StDow
    DsBuf(5) = DecToBcd(EdVal(3))
    DsBuf(6) = DecToBcd(EdVal(2))
    DsBuf(7) = DecToBcd(EdVal(1))
    DsWrite(0, 7)
    ClockRead
    ScreenStart
    ScreenStatus("Clock set", SCR_GOOD)
    ConsoleText("   Set ") : ConsoleLine(LogLine)
    ClockStore = 1
End Function

'''Sakamoto's month key, for the day of the week
Function MonthKey(In KeyMonth) As Byte
    ReadTable MonthKeys, KeyMonth, MonthKey
End Function

Table MonthKeys
    0
    3
    2
    5
    0
    3
    5
    1
    4
    6
    2
    4
End Table

// ----- The log file

'''Start the drive, mount it, and open RTCLOG.CSV to add to it (it is made if it is not there).
'''Returns 1 when the file is open, or 0 with the reason on the serial console.
'''FatInit (SDCInit, then FatMount) starts the card from the beginning, so this also works after a card is
'''pulled out and put back.
Function LogStart As Byte
    LogStart = 0
    ConsoleCRLF()
    If FatInit() <> FAT_OK Then
        If FatError = FAT_ERR_NO_DRIVE Then
            ConsoleText("   No card ") : ConsoleText(Str(SDCError)) : ConsoleText(" ")
            ConsoleLine(Str(SDCR1))    // SDCError, and the card's last answer (255: none)
        Else
            ConsoleText("   No FAT ") : ConsoleLine(Str(FatError))
        End If
        Exit Function
    End If
    If FatOpen("RTCLOG.CSV") <> FAT_OK Then
        ConsoleText("   Not opened ") : ConsoleLine(Str(FatError))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If FatCreated() = 1 Then
        LogText(SAMPLE_HEAD)            // a new file: the heading line first
        LogCRLF()
        ConsoleLine("   New file")
    Else
        ConsoleLine("   File open")
    End If
    LogStart = 1
End Function

'''A tap: counted, and "date,time,touch,screen,raw x,raw y,button" to the console and, while logging with the drive
'''ready, to the file
'''(the screen: 0 main, 1 menu, 2 black, 3 the clock screen; raw: TouchRaw and ClkRaw from MenuPressed). LogLine is made
'''again from the time: the main loop makes it again before it is used
Sub TouchLog(In TouchButton)
    TapCount++
    TouchToFile = 0
    If LogRun = 1 Then TouchToFile = LogReady
    ClockLine
    TouchText(LogLine)
    TouchText(",touch")
    TouchNum(ScrMode)
    TouchNum(TouchRaw)
    TouchNum(ClkRaw)
    TouchNum(TouchButton)
    ConsoleCRLF()
    If TouchToFile = 1 Then
        LogCRLF()
        ClockToFat
        If FatCommit() <> FAT_OK Then LogReady = 0      // the next sample starts the drive again
    End If
End Sub

'''TouchLog's line: a comma and a number
Sub TouchNum(In TouchValue As Word)
    TouchText(",")
    TouchText(Str(TouchValue))
End Sub

'''TouchLog's line: a string to the console and, while logging with the drive ready, to the file
Sub TouchText(In TouchString As String)
    ConsoleText(TouchString)
    If TouchToFile = 1 Then LogText(TouchString)
End Sub

'''Add LogLine to the file, after a "Restarted" line when samples were lost, and put it on the drive.
'''Returns 1 when FatCommit says it is on the drive, or 0 with the FatError on the serial console.
Function LogWrite As Byte
    LogWrite = 0
    If LogLost = 1 Then
        LogText("Restarted")            // the samples before this line were not written
        LogCRLF()
    End If
    LogText(LogLine)
    LogCRLF()
    ClockToFat                          // the file's date and time in the folder: now
    If FatCommit() <> FAT_OK Then
        ConsoleText("  FatError ") : ConsoleText(Str(FatError))
        Exit Function
    End If
    LogLost = 0
    LogWrite = 1
End Function

'''Add a string to the open file
Sub LogText(In LogString As String)
    Dim LogPos As Byte
    For LogPos = 1 To LogString(0)
        FatAppendByte(LogString(LogPos))
    Next
End Sub

'''End the line: CR LF
Sub LogCRLF
    FatAppendByte(13)
    FatAppendByte(10)
End Sub

// ----- The serial console

'''Send a string to the serial console
Sub ConsoleText(In ConsoleString As String)
    HSerPrint ConsoleString
End Sub

'''End the console line: CR LF
Sub ConsoleCRLF
    HSerPrintCRLF
End Sub

'''Send a string to the serial console and end the line (one call where there were two: less flash)
Sub ConsoleLine(In LineString As String)
    HSerPrint LineString
    HSerPrintCRLF
End Sub
